{"ts":"2026-08-11T13:58:00.698Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e3bd70efeed1d617d5fc3f49","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"max","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"planner","source":"inferred","confidence":"high","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["focus:pm-doxj","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-doxj","source":"inferred","confidence":"high","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["focus:pm-doxj","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.227","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-11T13:58:00.698Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-11T13:58:00.698Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Cross-reference 2026-08-11: this item owns counting the prose-named pairs that carry no edge. A promotion experiment recorded in full on pm-wmf72c establishes the precision ceiling for the obvious rule shape. At a same-sentence cue-immediately-before-identifier threshold the rule yields 8 candidates over the whole corpus and all 8 are false positives, because a cue identifies the relationship kind and object but never its subject, and in tracker prose the subject is usually a third identifier in the same sentence. So the 1,750-pair gap this item measures is not closable by a cue-and-object rule at any window size. The measurement this item owns should therefore report the pairs partitioned by whether the sentence contains an explicit subject identifier, because that partition is what decides how much of the gap is mechanically promotable at all."}]}],"before_hash":"425778940c34e8adb3efcc234698829abdfc74858eab0a59bb7ecf2f5fde9c3c","after_hash":"139faff24927f148274a9af70edfd55293c77f652ce1f7ce14278364e31c270f","message":"Record the precision ceiling measured for cue-and-object promotion"}
